1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,576
[Kawaii Monster]
<i>♪ Happy, lucky, wonderful ♪</i>

2
00:00:04,576 --> 00:00:05,576
All together now!

3
00:00:05,576 --> 00:00:07,067
<i>♪ Happy, lucky, wonderful ♪</i>

4
00:00:07,067 --> 00:00:09,767
<i>♪ Happy, lucky, wonderful ♪</i>

5
00:00:09,767 --> 00:00:13,880
- Make it cute!
- <i>♪ Happy, lucky, wonderful ♪</i>

6
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:17,433
- Make it super cute!
- <i>♪ Happy, lucky, wonderful ♪</i>

7
00:00:17,433 --> 00:00:20,000
- Say, cute!
- Cute!

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
- Cute!
- Cute!

9
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:27,033
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

10
00:00:27,733 --> 00:00:30,272
- Super cute!
- It is so cute!

11
00:00:30,272 --> 00:00:32,200
Look! Cute!

12
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,033
So cute...

13
00:00:34,033 --> 00:00:37,300
- Sorry for the wait.
- Cute!

14
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,820
Cute...

15
00:00:40,448 --> 00:00:43,160
Kusakabe? What is it?

16
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:45,167
Huh? Are you a staff member doing cosplay?

17
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:47,744
No, it's an undercover investigation
in the name of a gap part-time job.

18
00:00:47,744 --> 00:00:50,101
What? Undercover investigation?

19
00:00:50,101 --> 00:00:52,840
Excuse me! Could you take a picture for us?

20
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:54,767
Sure. Go ahead.

21
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:57,567
Say cheese!

22
00:00:57,567 --> 00:00:59,067
Here you go.

23
00:00:59,067 --> 00:01:02,033
Well, Miss, would you like to
be in the photo with us?

24
00:01:02,033 --> 00:01:04,033
That's true. She is cute.

25
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:06,016
- Come on! Let's take a photo!
- No, I'm... Well...

26
00:01:06,016 --> 00:01:07,712
- Let's take a photo!
- Alright. Alright. Alright.

27
00:01:07,712 --> 00:01:10,933
I'll take it. Come on.

28
00:01:10,933 --> 00:01:12,960
Okay, do a cute pose!

29
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,688
- Cute... Wait.
- Ready, set.

30
00:01:14,688 --> 00:01:18,280
So cute!

31
00:01:19,392 --> 00:01:21,392
What?

32
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,760
I mean, why am I like this...

33
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,520
I want to do it! I love it!

34
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,600
I just can't stop loving it!

35
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,467
Then just do it!

36
00:01:31,467 --> 00:01:33,733
I'm in 'let's do this together' mode.

37
00:01:33,733 --> 00:01:37,248
I'm in 'let's make it a huge hit' mode!

38
00:01:37,248 --> 00:01:38,633
I'll do it!

39
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:41,608
I'll do it too!

40
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:47,633
Are we going to do it together?

41
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:51,467
I'm going to do consulting, right?

42
00:01:51,467 --> 00:01:53,120
Do it?

43
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,616
Do it.

44
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:57,640
Do it.

45
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,712
Probably, I'll do it.

46
00:02:01,133 --> 00:02:03,880
[Seo Design]
So, Mr. Seo, at your request,

47
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:05,833
- starting today, I will be consulting...
- No, no, no.

48
00:02:05,833 --> 00:02:07,768
My request? You said you wanted to do it.

49
00:02:07,768 --> 00:02:08,768
You said you wanted to do it

50
00:02:08,768 --> 00:02:10,016
- while bursting into tears.
- Well...

51
00:02:10,016 --> 00:02:12,200
It's liquid. Just some liquid
coming out of my eyes.

52
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:16,400
That's enough.
Anyway, we're doing this, right?

53
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:20,100
Well, though you're the one
who brought it up.

54
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,968
[Consultant Agreement]
This will be a formal consulting agreement.

55
00:02:23,968 --> 00:02:26,856
But before that,
there's something I need to tell you.

56
00:02:26,967 --> 00:02:30,900
I have no experience being passionate about
or absorbed in something.

57
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,920
I've never even liked a character before.

58
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:36,400
Perhaps because of that, I don't have
any sense of what 'cute' means either.

59
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:40,680
So I'm currently infiltrating various
cute-related facilities to investigate.

60
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,792
Like this.

61
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:47,776
I mean, you want to consult
without even understanding what cute is.

62
00:02:47,776 --> 00:02:49,267
That's some nerve.

63
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:52,800
Even if I don't understand cute,
by looking at characters and goods,

64
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:57,833
I can understand the target, aim, cost rate,
and other business elements and numbers.

65
00:02:57,833 --> 00:03:01,820
So you don't need to worry about that.
Or rather, I hope you can trust me on that.

66
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:04,800
I have a policy of not trusting people.

67
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,168
Okay, but for the sake of

68
00:03:07,168 --> 00:03:09,767
- smooth business operations...
- My grandma used to say that

69
00:03:09,767 --> 00:03:12,767
never trust anyone
who tells you to trust them.

70
00:03:12,767 --> 00:03:16,833
- Well, she's right, but...
- Now then!

71
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,460
[Consulting Fee]
Impress me with your results!

72
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:22,480
What? What! What?

73
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,352
- What!
- Well, with this,

74
00:03:24,352 --> 00:03:27,833
I'll be ordering you around
to my heart's content.

75
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:33,160
- But you don't have any work...
- And whose fault do you think that is?

76
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:37,160
I'm sorry. Let me confirm here.

77
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:43,776
I struggled with it too.
My savings are practically nothing.

78
00:03:43,776 --> 00:03:47,267
But I swapped my usual big, cheap bread

79
00:03:47,267 --> 00:03:49,567
- for this small, cheap bread...
- It's not enough.

80
00:03:49,567 --> 00:03:50,912
- What?
- It's not enough.

81
00:03:50,912 --> 00:03:55,360
Oh, but I don't know
the market rate for consulting.

82
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,824
But it's kind of like
a video streaming subscription, right?

83
00:03:57,824 --> 00:04:00,840
For a six-month contract,
it's 30 million yen.

84
00:04:01,367 --> 00:04:03,860
You're a hyena! That's hyena-ism!

85
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:06,967
That said, that figure is
for major corporations.

86
00:04:06,967 --> 00:04:08,416
And there's also the matter of Takai Create.

87
00:04:08,416 --> 00:04:10,200
So first, let me compensate you for that.

88
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:13,384
After that, you can pay me
based on the results.

89
00:04:13,980 --> 00:04:17,367
Alright, I've also prepared a job for you.

90
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:19,030
A bakery called Oyama Bakery

91
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:20,700
[Oyama Bakery]
is commemorating its 50th anniversary.

92
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:25,033
They want an original character for the shop,
and they'd like you to design it.

93
00:04:25,033 --> 00:04:26,560
Alright, though I don't really get it...

94
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,928
Understood. Well then, please sign here.

95
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:37,280
A written pledge?

96
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:42,496
Well, just some rules from me, too.
Common sense, got it?

97
00:04:42,496 --> 00:04:45,100
Don't talk about Merry in front of me.

98
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:48,400
Don't talk about Omishima.
Don't talk about Cynical Molco.

99
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:50,144
Don't tell anyone that liquid
came out of my eyes.

100
00:04:50,144 --> 00:04:55,016
If you tell them, you're fired.
And when I say fired, I mean fired.

101
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:08,520
All right. And with that,
our contract is sealed.

102
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:14,216
Mr. Seo, before I begin consulting,
I have one important question.

103
00:05:14,767 --> 00:05:18,133
What is our goal?

104
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:22,140
What do you want to do?
What do you want to create?

105
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:24,620
If we are to create a new character,

106
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:27,800
I think it will also be
connected to that concept.

107
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:31,180
Please think it over carefully.

108
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,568
What's our goal?

109
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,872
Goal...

110
00:05:38,633 --> 00:05:40,533
What's our goal?

111
00:05:40,533 --> 00:05:43,780
<i>Cynical Molco is very popular, isn't it?</i>

112
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:45,408
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

113
00:05:45,408 --> 00:05:47,700
<i>We are quite surprised ourselves.</i>

114
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:51,033
<i>How can one create such a hit product?</i>

115
00:05:51,033 --> 00:05:53,460
[Merry President, Takumi Omishima]
You just called it a hit product,

116
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:56,900
but we do not think of
our characters as products.

117
00:05:56,900 --> 00:06:01,460
[This is where a new era begins]
They're more like our children.

118
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:03,920
<i>Like our children.</i>

119
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:07,767
This one is like a child to me.

120
00:06:07,767 --> 00:06:09,367
It's okay.

121
00:06:09,367 --> 00:06:12,300
Please trust me...

122
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,133
<i>The same goes for Molco.</i>

123
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:16,384
With the initial settings and designs
you came up with,

124
00:06:16,384 --> 00:06:17,568
<i>it didn't seem like they would sell well.</i>

125
00:06:17,568 --> 00:06:20,567
<i>So I made some adjustments.</i>

126
00:06:20,567 --> 00:06:23,420
As a result, it became
an unprecedentedly huge hit.

127
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:26,700
<i>That very ruthlessness is
what made them evolve.</i>

128
00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:32,333
<i>And I believe that evolution
is what led to this hit.</i>

129
00:06:34,333 --> 00:06:37,467
Evolution?

130
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,264
- Well...
- He doesn't get it.

131
00:06:39,264 --> 00:06:40,867
He doesn't get anything.

132
00:06:40,867 --> 00:06:42,600
- Well, no...
- He killed it!

133
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:45,096
This guy killed it!

134
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:50,856
- Cheese! Yeah!
- Let's do a heart too.

135
00:06:52,033 --> 00:06:54,533
Cute?

136
00:06:54,533 --> 00:06:57,384
Molco!

137
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:03,800
Hey, that plushie will get wet. Here.

138
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:09,000
Because Molco, who's usually all "hmph,"
goes "hmph" at the very end.

139
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,533
Then everyone goes "hmph,"
and I go "hmph" too.

140
00:07:11,533 --> 00:07:14,467
I see. "Hmph", huh?

141
00:07:14,467 --> 00:07:18,120
Hey, your nose is running.

142
00:07:20,608 --> 00:07:22,792
Molco.

143
00:07:25,152 --> 00:07:27,302
Molco.

144
00:07:29,733 --> 00:07:31,967
Oh, sorry, you're studying.

145
00:07:31,967 --> 00:07:37,067
No, it's fine.
I was just thinking that it's love.

146
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:38,667
Love...

147
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:40,567
Oh, no.

148
00:07:40,567 --> 00:07:42,336
Oh, it's getting late.

149
00:07:42,336 --> 00:07:44,192
- Aren't you sleepy? You okay?
- I'm not sleepy.

150
00:07:44,192 --> 00:07:47,432
Oh, yeah, I think I'm okay.

151
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,667
S-S-So, how is it? The world of
creating characters as a business?

152
00:07:51,667 --> 00:07:55,848
Well, it's tougher than I thought.

153
00:07:57,367 --> 00:08:02,167
First, the producer or project leader
decides what kind of character to make,

154
00:08:02,167 --> 00:08:04,467
and who to target.

155
00:08:04,467 --> 00:08:08,180
Next, a character designer
creates the design,

156
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:11,720
and while they devise the name
and setting, the character...

157
00:08:13,067 --> 00:08:18,240
Well, anyway, it's tough,
and only a handful succeed.

158
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:22,720
But basically, manga, anime, games,

159
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:25,100
they are also
character creation businesses, right?

160
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:28,133
Well, but those at least
have some predictability,

161
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,144
since they're already popular.

162
00:08:30,144 --> 00:08:33,420
But succeeding with
a so-called mascot character,

163
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:37,260
like Hello Kitty, is quite difficult.

164
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:39,933
Oh, but isn't Cynical Molco like that too?

165
00:08:39,933 --> 00:08:45,367
Well, the success of that character is

166
00:08:45,367 --> 00:08:47,900
[Character Business Revolution]
thanks to this person's acumen,

167
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:52,200
[By Takumi Omishima]
or rather, his ability to sniff out a hit.

168
00:08:55,233 --> 00:08:58,167
<i>This one is like a child to me.</i>

169
00:08:58,167 --> 00:09:00,267
<i>It's okay.</i>

170
00:09:00,267 --> 00:09:04,168
Please trust me...

171
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:07,208
Wait a minute!

172
00:09:12,512 --> 00:09:13,600
Hmph, hmph, hmph.

173
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,433
Who are you?

174
00:09:15,433 --> 00:09:18,504
- Mol...
- Molco!

175
00:09:19,616 --> 00:09:22,408
- Mol...
- Hmph.

176
00:09:23,584 --> 00:09:24,704
Hmph, hmph.

177
00:09:24,704 --> 00:09:26,633
- Mol...
- Stop!

178
00:09:26,633 --> 00:09:28,840
Mol...

179
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:31,174
Stop it!

180
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,856
Molco!

181
00:09:44,967 --> 00:09:48,033
Good morning.

182
00:09:52,928 --> 00:09:55,584
<i>Hmph, hmph, hmph.</i>

183
00:09:55,584 --> 00:09:58,312
<i>Hmph, hmph, hmph.</i>

184
00:10:00,467 --> 00:10:03,880
About that goal business.

185
00:10:04,267 --> 00:10:05,433
Yes?

186
00:10:05,433 --> 00:10:08,800
My goal is vengeance for Full Tummy Molco,

187
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:12,500
who was killed
before it ever saw the light of day!

188
00:10:14,567 --> 00:10:21,832
V-e-n-g-e-a-n-c-e.

189
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,520
Vengeance!

190
00:10:25,664 --> 00:10:27,688
Vengeance?

191
00:10:41,167 --> 00:10:42,784
[Episode 2]

192
00:10:42,784 --> 00:10:44,544
[Hello, Ms. Anna Kusakabe.
Need me to check anything for you?]

193
00:10:44,544 --> 00:10:46,304
[What does it mean, aiming for vengeance?]

194
00:10:46,304 --> 00:10:50,100
<i>Vengeance is an illegal act in modern times.</i>

195
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:53,067
What is this exchange?

196
00:10:53,567 --> 00:10:57,167
Is it done? The vengeance plan?

197
00:10:57,167 --> 00:10:59,467
Sorry, not yet.

198
00:10:59,467 --> 00:11:03,168
I mean, my specialty
is management strategy support

199
00:11:03,168 --> 00:11:05,216
- and operational efficiency...
- Is it done?

200
00:11:05,216 --> 00:11:07,848
The vengeance plan.

201
00:11:08,867 --> 00:11:11,467
I'll do my best.

202
00:11:11,467 --> 00:11:15,560
[Vengeance! Chushingura]

203
00:11:20,352 --> 00:11:22,800
Ms. Kusakabe?

204
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:28,160
Oh, you're from Merry.
Well... Mr. Hirose, right?

205
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:29,248
Yes.

206
00:11:29,248 --> 00:11:32,520
Molco's autograph session
is happening in the back right now.

207
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:36,000
- It's Molco!
- Hello.

208
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,024
Here.

209
00:11:37,024 --> 00:11:40,600
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

210
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,733
By the way, are you still
working with Mr. Seo?

211
00:11:43,733 --> 00:11:46,700
Yes. I'm officially working with him now.
I'm the consultant.

212
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:49,833
I see. That's good.

213
00:11:49,833 --> 00:11:51,267
Oh, yes. Well...

214
00:11:51,267 --> 00:11:53,367
I wanted to say again, I'm truly sorry

215
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:55,900
for all the trouble I caused
at the competition the other day.

216
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:59,167
It's fine. That ended up
being canceled, anyway.

217
00:11:59,167 --> 00:12:01,233
Could it be that

218
00:12:01,233 --> 00:12:05,533
- it was because of the mess we caused?
- No, no, not at all.

219
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:10,952
In the end, nothing really clicked,
so nobody ended up qualifying.

220
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:14,320
But is that okay?

221
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:17,167
The shopping mall is going to be built,
and it needs a character...

222
00:12:17,167 --> 00:12:18,800
That's true.

223
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:22,167
So, I contacted
the organizing company a while ago,

224
00:12:22,167 --> 00:12:26,120
and now among the higher-ups...

225
00:12:26,767 --> 00:12:31,100
they're saying that they'd like
Mr. Seo to draw it again.

226
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:33,260
- Mr. Seo?
- Hey! Wait, wait!

227
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:36,160
<i>♪ Se, se, se, yoi, yoi, yoi ♪</i>

228
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:38,304
<i>♪ Chitter-chatter, chitter-chat ♪</i>

229
00:12:38,304 --> 00:12:39,304
Excuse me.

230
00:12:39,304 --> 00:12:41,960
<i>♪ Chitter-chatter-chat ♪</i>

231
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,456
Sorry for the wait.

232
00:12:43,456 --> 00:12:46,927
[Vengeance Plan]
Here is the vengeance plan.

233
00:12:54,667 --> 00:12:56,000
This is from the other day...

234
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,733
Creating a character for
the shopping mall to be built in Nerima.

235
00:12:58,733 --> 00:13:01,960
The client says they want you
to draw the character again.

236
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:04,933
However, when the character is announced,

237
00:13:04,933 --> 00:13:08,867
they want to prominently feature your title
as the designer of Cynical Molco.

238
00:13:08,867 --> 00:13:12,200
- And we'll need Merry's permission...
- You want me to...

239
00:13:12,767 --> 00:13:17,320
If you're serious about this...

240
00:13:20,767 --> 00:13:24,667
you're hell-bound.

241
00:13:26,767 --> 00:13:30,533
The official name of this project is...

242
00:13:31,467 --> 00:13:35,440
the Shopping Mall Character Project,
Volume Two.

243
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:38,033
- It's Volume Two!
- Two?

244
00:13:38,033 --> 00:13:41,733
Volume One is the character creation
for the Itabashi shopping mall,

245
00:13:41,733 --> 00:13:44,616
and the creator is...

246
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:46,400
[Merry Co., Ltd.]
Merry.

247
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,992
If the Nerima character you create

248
00:13:48,992 --> 00:13:54,233
becomes more popular than
Merry's Itabashi character...

249
00:13:55,333 --> 00:13:58,667
It'd be successful vengeance!

250
00:13:58,667 --> 00:14:02,200
The fee is high, and if you establish
a track record on a big project like this,

251
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,133
it will certainly be advantageous
for you in the future.

252
00:14:04,133 --> 00:14:07,033
Even though you just broke
one of the rules around here...

253
00:14:07,033 --> 00:14:09,064
[Don't talk about Merry]

254
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,900
I forgive you.

255
00:14:14,033 --> 00:14:17,992
Just watch. I'll make Nerima defeat Itabashi.

256
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,952
Defeat it!

257
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:26,800
I'll make Nerima defeat Itabashi!

258
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:29,060
[Nerima Official Anime Character: Nerimaru]
<i>♪ I was supposed to do ♪</i>

259
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:31,320
[Itabashi Tourism Character: Rinrin]
<i>♪ Proper consulting ♪</i>

260
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:35,880
<i>♪ Seeking vengeance at a shopping mall ♪</i>

261
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:40,300
<i>♪ I was supposed to do cute consulting ♪</i>

262
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:45,700
<i>♪ Vengeance, in Nerima, against Itabashi ♪</i>

263
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:54,133
<i>♪ An amateur girl who
doesn't know the right answer ♪</i>

264
00:14:54,980 --> 00:15:03,600
<i>♪ An amateur girl oozing anxiety ♪</i>

265
00:15:06,067 --> 00:15:07,392
[Oyama Bakery]
Oh, hello. This is Oyama Bakery.

266
00:15:07,392 --> 00:15:08,392
Thank you for your patronage.

267
00:15:08,392 --> 00:15:09,733
- Hello.
- Hello.

268
00:15:09,733 --> 00:15:12,467
Well, is it done yet? Our character?

269
00:15:12,467 --> 00:15:16,033
Well... the deadline
hasn't passed yet, right?

270
00:15:16,033 --> 00:15:21,600
I'm sorry. No, I was just
curious about how it's going.

271
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:24,433
Vengeance...

272
00:15:24,433 --> 00:15:27,033
Vengeance.

273
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:32,320
The designer is working on it right now.

274
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:33,536
I see, I see!

275
00:15:33,536 --> 00:15:35,584
[First 50 visitors get a free]
Well, it's our first time having

276
00:15:35,584 --> 00:15:36,736
[original Oyama character keychain]
an original store character.

277
00:15:36,736 --> 00:15:39,533
Well... I'm just really excited about it.

278
00:15:39,533 --> 00:15:42,560
<i>Can you imagine an original
character for Oyama Bakery?</i>

279
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:45,500
<i>That's exactly why I'd want to get one.</i>

280
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,600
Well, you see,
it's our 50th anniversary coming up.

281
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:52,240
I was thinking we could give them out
to our regular customers and kids.

282
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:53,700
- Right?
- Yeah, I want one.

283
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:57,536
Understood. We'll do our best
to meet your expectations.

284
00:15:57,536 --> 00:15:59,136
Excuse us.

285
00:15:59,136 --> 00:16:02,792
Vengeance... Vengeance...

286
00:16:02,967 --> 00:16:06,867
- Vengeance... Vengeance...
- Well, Mr. Seo?

287
00:16:06,867 --> 00:16:09,152
Mr. Seo!

288
00:16:09,152 --> 00:16:11,300
What? Why are you shouting all of a sudden?

289
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:14,433
The Nerima project is fine,
but what about the other job?

290
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:17,767
The bakery, right?
What, you thought I hadn't done it?

291
00:16:17,767 --> 00:16:20,667
- No, it's not that...
- You surprised me.

292
00:16:20,667 --> 00:16:24,936
I thought maybe you didn't trust me. Yikes.

293
00:16:26,733 --> 00:16:29,500
Vengeance.

294
00:16:44,467 --> 00:16:46,016
It's done.

295
00:16:46,016 --> 00:16:47,367
Good morning.

296
00:16:47,367 --> 00:16:50,620
I drew it. The Nerima one, I drew it.

297
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:52,433
What do you think? Is it cute? Cute, right?

298
00:16:52,433 --> 00:16:56,433
Well... It's a bit different from
the image the client is looking for.

299
00:16:56,433 --> 00:17:01,300
What? Different? What?
Where? Where is it different?

300
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:04,333
More importantly, the deadline for
Oyama Bakery is approaching.

301
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:06,432
- How's the progress?
- I'm...

302
00:17:06,432 --> 00:17:08,767
I'm the type who doesn't want anyone
to see my work in progress.

303
00:17:08,767 --> 00:17:11,424
Is that so? But I will see it.

304
00:17:11,424 --> 00:17:15,968
Wait! You really don't trust me! Wait!

305
00:17:15,968 --> 00:17:17,233
[Oyama Bakery]

306
00:17:17,233 --> 00:17:19,900
I'm clicking now.

307
00:17:21,633 --> 00:17:24,633
Is this...

308
00:17:24,633 --> 00:17:27,300
Is this hijiki seaweed?

309
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:31,008
I'm really sorry.
Please give us a little more time.

310
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:33,400
No, it's fine.

311
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,440
Guess the designer really cares that much.

312
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:38,720
What? There isn't any Oyama Bakery keychain?

313
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,744
- There isn't?
- There isn't?

314
00:17:39,744 --> 00:17:42,784
No, no, no, that's not true! There is! Right?

315
00:17:42,784 --> 00:17:46,376
- Look forward to it, okay?
- Yes!

316
00:17:58,667 --> 00:18:01,152
Hello, this is Kusakabe from
Horai Consulting... No, I mean...

317
00:18:01,152 --> 00:18:03,784
<i>I finally drew it.</i>

318
00:18:03,967 --> 00:18:07,067
- The one for Mr. Oyama?
- I drew the Nerima one.

319
00:18:07,067 --> 00:18:11,136
Want to see? I'll send it. There, I sent it.

320
00:18:11,136 --> 00:18:16,967
Well... Is that thing on its head a helmet?

321
00:18:16,967 --> 00:18:19,600
It's a hat. A hat.

322
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:23,433
So, what do you think?
Is it cute? Cute, right?

323
00:18:23,433 --> 00:18:28,940
Well... I'll gather some more
information about Nerima.

324
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:31,100
We can incorporate that
and adjust the design a bit more.

325
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:33,180
Adjust? Why?

326
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:34,400
<i>Why is an adjustment necessary?</i>

327
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:39,340
Well... just to be doubly sure.
To aim for something more solid.

328
00:18:39,712 --> 00:18:40,733
All right, fine.

329
00:18:40,733 --> 00:18:44,424
By the way, what about Oyama Bakery?

330
00:18:47,744 --> 00:18:50,344
[Seo Design]

331
00:18:51,467 --> 00:18:52,600
Good morning.

332
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:55,767
I drew it. I drew it! I drew it!

333
00:18:55,767 --> 00:18:58,700
Oh, great! Then I'll take it
to Mr. Oyama right away...

334
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:01,767
What do you think?
Cute, right? This is the idea.

335
00:19:01,767 --> 00:19:04,240
Send it. Just send it to them.

336
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:06,267
I can't send this.

337
00:19:06,267 --> 00:19:07,360
What?

338
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:10,833
Because it's Chushingura, isn't it?

339
00:19:10,833 --> 00:19:14,400
It's even more Kuranosuke
than Kuranosuke Oishi himself, isn't it?

340
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:16,576
[Vengeance! Chushingura]
How and where is it Kuranosuke?

341
00:19:16,576 --> 00:19:19,784
Anyway, I can't send that.
I can't just send it to them like that.

342
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,700
Fine, then.

343
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:25,767
Wait a minute! Wait, wait!

344
00:19:25,767 --> 00:19:27,267
[Send]
I'm clicking!

345
00:19:27,267 --> 00:19:28,992
[Sent]
Ah! It's done...

346
00:19:28,992 --> 00:19:32,600
You sent it? Kuranosuke? You sent Kuranosuke?

347
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:36,500
With this, vengeance...

348
00:19:38,933 --> 00:19:42,784
Mr. Seo? Mr. Seo? Seo...

349
00:19:42,784 --> 00:19:47,560
Hey, wake up! Oyama Bakery. Oyama Bakery!

350
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:50,040
Molco...

351
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:52,367
[Sinful Chestnut]
I am truly sorry.

352
00:19:52,367 --> 00:19:56,767
In three more days... No, two more days,
we'll be able to finish it.

353
00:19:56,767 --> 00:19:58,400
Please.

354
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,840
Ms. Kusakabe.

355
00:20:01,167 --> 00:20:06,433
I'm sorry, but I'm going to ask someone else.

356
00:20:06,433 --> 00:20:10,600
I really want to make it in time
for our 50th anniversary.

357
00:20:26,432 --> 00:20:30,312
[Oyama Bakery
has terminated the contract with us]

358
00:20:43,952 --> 00:20:44,952
[Latest Video: Getting Close to the Real Face
of Merry President Takumi Omishima!]

359
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:46,952
[His Resolve as a Leader
and Passion for Merry]

360
00:20:49,088 --> 00:20:54,133
<i>This week, we'd like to ask you
about your social circle.</i>

361
00:20:54,133 --> 00:20:55,552
[Merry President, Takumi Omishima]
<i>This is Ms. Kumi Sakoda,</i>

362
00:20:55,552 --> 00:20:58,208
[Kitchen Sakoda President, Kumi Sakoda]
<i>the president of that hot topic right now,</i>

363
00:20:58,208 --> 00:21:00,288
[Kitchen Sakoda]
<i>Kitchen Sakoda, isn't it?</i>

364
00:21:00,288 --> 00:21:03,400
<i>I heard that you're very close.</i>

365
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:04,880
<i>That's right.</i>

366
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:09,700
<i>We have a mutual acquaintance
who introduced us.</i>

367
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:12,672
<i>She's a very powerful person.</i>

368
00:21:12,672 --> 00:21:16,520
<i>We want to spread the charm
of Kitchen Sakoda to the world.</i>

369
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:22,528
Why was she with Omishima...

370
00:21:22,528 --> 00:21:27,232
- Welcome.
- <i>Lunchtime, dinnertime,</i>

371
00:21:27,232 --> 00:21:30,464
<i>enjoyable days with family and friends.</i>

372
00:21:30,464 --> 00:21:34,080
- <i>Welcome to Hot! Hot!</i>
- Hello, good morning.

373
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:37,740
Hey, there's something I want to ask you.

374
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:41,600
Oh, I'm in the middle of something
right now. Perhaps tomorrow?

375
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:43,700
<i>What are you in the middle of?</i>

376
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:45,992
It's a trade secret.

377
00:21:46,176 --> 00:21:48,456
<i>So, tomorrow, then.</i>

378
00:21:48,672 --> 00:21:52,968
<i>There are juicy meat dishes available...</i>

379
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:55,616
Hot! Hot!

380
00:21:55,616 --> 00:22:01,000
You see, humans unconditionally
find round things cute.

381
00:22:03,233 --> 00:22:05,033
I knew it.

382
00:22:05,033 --> 00:22:07,580
Meeting secretly with Merry...

383
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:11,072
When you reach my level, you will know...
Is something wrong?

384
00:22:11,072 --> 00:22:15,380
No, I just felt something like
murderous intent.

385
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:16,480
What?

386
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:22,056
Meeting secretly with Merry...

387
00:22:25,433 --> 00:22:27,700
- What?
- Is something wrong?

388
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:31,600
The company behind the Nerima
shopping mall wants to meet.

389
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,960
What?

390
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:35,860
[Neri-Morusuke]

391
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:46,632
It's great, isn't it?

392
00:22:47,467 --> 00:22:51,133
This edgy vibe is just brutal.

393
00:22:51,133 --> 00:22:54,120
It blows right past all the rules.

394
00:22:54,533 --> 00:22:56,400
It really strikes a chord!

395
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:58,467
It means...

396
00:22:58,467 --> 00:23:03,016
Let's go with this for Nerima.

397
00:23:05,220 --> 00:23:06,500
Thank you very much.

398
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:07,744
No, thank you.

399
00:23:07,744 --> 00:23:09,700
- What do you think?
- This is the only way, right?

400
00:23:09,700 --> 00:23:11,733
You said it.

401
00:23:11,733 --> 00:23:14,667
I'm sorry.

402
00:23:14,667 --> 00:23:18,100
I really don't understand.

403
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:24,008
What are characters, anyway?

404
00:23:25,376 --> 00:23:27,400
Fired.

405
00:23:27,633 --> 00:23:29,733
Huh? Neck?
[*"Fired" and "neck" sound close in Japanese]

406
00:23:29,733 --> 00:23:32,060
Oh, Kuranosuke's?

407
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:33,600
Dismissal.

408
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:36,200
Dis... Dismissal?

409
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:39,900
Because I realized I can manage on my own.

410
00:23:39,900 --> 00:23:42,467
Also, a consultant who doesn't
understand cute is a burden.

411
00:23:42,467 --> 00:23:45,056
Above all, I can't trust you.

412
00:23:45,056 --> 00:23:48,296
You're secretly connected to Omishima.

413
00:23:50,833 --> 00:23:52,936
Dismissal.

414
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:00,867
Zapaan!

415
00:24:00,867 --> 00:24:03,333
How do you feel? Did it wash away?
That cloudy feeling?

416
00:24:03,333 --> 00:24:06,200
No, it's stuck. It's clogged in my throat!

417
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:08,160
Excuse me! A large Zapaan shochu
with sweet potato!

418
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:09,840
Another shochu, and another one of this too.

419
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:11,616
- Okay. Coming right up.
- But how did he know about

420
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:12,767
Mr. Omishima and me?

421
00:24:12,767 --> 00:24:15,267
Hey, isn't it okay already?

422
00:24:15,267 --> 00:24:17,480
You're fired, so that means
you're free, right?

423
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:19,833
Want to go to Yamashiroya sometime?

424
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:23,200
Do you know that place?
They have lots of cute stuff!

425
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:25,864
How about it? This Sunday?

426
00:24:28,267 --> 00:24:31,112
Sunday's not great for me.

427
00:24:34,100 --> 00:24:36,400
- Thank you for your patronage.
- Mr. Oyama, excuse me. I'd like to switch.

428
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:39,400
- Oh, okay. Please go ahead.
- Alright.

429
00:24:56,416 --> 00:24:58,784
Vengeance.

430
00:24:58,784 --> 00:25:01,384
Vengeance.

431
00:25:02,267 --> 00:25:04,933
Vengeance.

432
00:25:04,933 --> 00:25:07,400
Vengeance.

433
00:25:10,460 --> 00:25:12,200
Do you have a minute?

434
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:14,240
- Hey! Hey!
- No way!

435
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:16,224
I said, no way! I don't want to,
not even for a minute!

436
00:25:16,224 --> 00:25:17,568
Understood. Then, is five hours okay?

437
00:25:17,568 --> 00:25:18,967
What are you thinking?

438
00:25:18,967 --> 00:25:21,800
Then six hours... Seven hours.

439
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:23,167
Why is it increasing?

440
00:25:23,167 --> 00:25:27,967
- Your face is like The Shining...
- Eight hours... Nine hours... Ten hours!

441
00:25:27,967 --> 00:25:31,040
Eleven...

442
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:32,640
What?

443
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:35,488
Oyama Bakery is celebrating
its 50th anniversary.

444
00:25:35,488 --> 00:25:38,100
Welcome.

445
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:40,584
It's Oyama Bakery.

446
00:25:42,267 --> 00:25:45,152
- We're handing out balloons.
- Can you see the poster?

447
00:25:45,152 --> 00:25:48,400
[Original Oyama Character Keychain]
It's Oyama Bakery's 50th anniversary.

448
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:51,000
[Canceled]
Canceled...

449
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:52,067
Why?

450
00:25:52,067 --> 00:25:55,633
I heard they looked for another designer
after that, but couldn't find one.

451
00:25:55,633 --> 00:25:58,400
And the AI designs didn't click either,
so in the end...

452
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:01,216
We're having an event today. Please go ahead.

453
00:26:01,216 --> 00:26:05,033
I still don't understand what is cute.

454
00:26:05,033 --> 00:26:07,872
And I'm an amateur in the character business.
But I do know this.

455
00:26:07,872 --> 00:26:09,056
You came! Take it!

456
00:26:09,056 --> 00:26:13,000
- Come on. Take the balloon.
- What? No character keychains?

457
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,600
I'm sorry. It can't be helped.

458
00:26:14,600 --> 00:26:19,560
- Balloons are nice too.
- We prioritized our own selfish feelings.

459
00:26:20,267 --> 00:26:23,048
We didn't face Mr. Oyama properly.

460
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:28,520
And for someone,

461
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:34,056
we robbed them of a chance
to encounter a lifelong love.

462
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:38,760
It's done.

463
00:26:39,433 --> 00:26:42,024
What are you drawing?

464
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:46,888
You're good! Amazing!

465
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:49,672
Good!

466
00:26:54,016 --> 00:26:56,832
Sticker. Put a sticker
on your favorite bread.

467
00:26:56,832 --> 00:26:59,133
Mr. Seo?

468
00:26:59,133 --> 00:27:00,864
- Hey!
- Oyama Bakery is celebrating

469
00:27:00,864 --> 00:27:02,880
- Mr. Seo!
- its 50th anniversary!

470
00:27:02,880 --> 00:27:07,133
- We're a delicious, delicious bakery!
- Excuse me.

471
00:27:07,133 --> 00:27:10,733
I'm Seo, the designer, and this time...

472
00:27:10,733 --> 00:27:14,336
No, no, no... No, it's not that...
That kind of thing...

473
00:27:14,336 --> 00:27:16,032
You see, there are children here.

474
00:27:16,032 --> 00:27:19,648
No clue what the Oyama
character keychain looks like.

475
00:27:19,648 --> 00:27:21,568
Can I borrow a pen?

476
00:27:21,568 --> 00:27:23,936
- I like the bread one.
- Stop it.

477
00:27:23,936 --> 00:27:26,833
- Or that...
- All kinds are good.

478
00:27:26,833 --> 00:27:28,864
Can I have a balloon?

479
00:27:28,864 --> 00:27:30,920
Sure.

480
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:41,090
Impressive!

481
00:27:41,850 --> 00:27:44,110
So good!

482
00:27:50,933 --> 00:27:52,736
Here.

483
00:27:52,736 --> 00:27:55,800
It's old man Oyama! Old man bread loaf!

484
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:57,088
Awesome!

485
00:27:57,088 --> 00:27:59,360
Draw one for me too! An old man hot dog.

486
00:27:59,360 --> 00:28:01,888
- Great drawing!
- Next, draw me a melon bread, too!

487
00:28:01,888 --> 00:28:03,933
- That's good.
- Look, look!

488
00:28:03,933 --> 00:28:06,336
It really is amazing, isn't it?

489
00:28:06,336 --> 00:28:08,488
Awesome!

490
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:11,600
Here you go.

491
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:14,433
- Old man!
- Old man hot dog!

492
00:28:14,433 --> 00:28:15,744
Can I draw these too?

493
00:28:15,744 --> 00:28:17,184
- Hold on.
- Oh, okay.

494
00:28:17,184 --> 00:28:18,752
Amazing.

495
00:28:18,752 --> 00:28:21,460
- Awesome.
- Amazing, amazing.

496
00:28:21,460 --> 00:28:26,088
<i>Characters really are amazing, aren't they?</i>

497
00:28:27,133 --> 00:28:32,367
<i>They turn something ordinary
into something special.</i>

498
00:28:32,367 --> 00:28:36,904
And both the receiver
and the giver become happy.

499
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:45,160
Well...

500
00:28:46,067 --> 00:28:48,808
About Mr. Omishima,

501
00:28:50,567 --> 00:28:53,416
I should have told you properly.

502
00:28:53,967 --> 00:28:59,533
Of course, he was just a client
from my consulting days,

503
00:28:59,533 --> 00:29:02,760
but I just thought it
might be better not to mention it.

504
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:05,256
But...

505
00:29:06,533 --> 00:29:09,960
that might have been
a selfish judgment on my part.

506
00:29:11,567 --> 00:29:13,824
I'm sorry.

507
00:29:13,824 --> 00:29:15,880
Forget it.

508
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:20,424
Excuse me.

509
00:29:21,504 --> 00:29:24,392
We're not done talking yet.

510
00:29:28,667 --> 00:29:30,984
Well...

511
00:29:33,152 --> 00:29:36,872
[Mi! Berry Good!]

512
00:29:37,167 --> 00:29:39,700
So,

513
00:29:40,533 --> 00:29:43,048
does that mean this character
is also no good?

514
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:45,467
Yes.

515
00:29:45,467 --> 00:29:47,600
You just said it earlier.

516
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:50,933
Characters turn something ordinary
into something special,

517
00:29:50,933 --> 00:29:54,024
and make both the receiver
and the giver happy.

518
00:29:54,944 --> 00:29:57,352
Would you be happy to receive this?

519
00:30:01,667 --> 00:30:04,552
I want to redo it.

520
00:30:06,180 --> 00:30:09,233
So, you know, make that kind of contact.

521
00:30:09,233 --> 00:30:12,467
- But I'm fired...
- As some people say,

522
00:30:12,467 --> 00:30:16,800
once trust is lost, it takes
several times more, whatever,

523
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:21,992
to restore it, or something like that.

524
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:24,424
So...

525
00:30:24,576 --> 00:30:27,656
Do... Do your best.

526
00:30:31,872 --> 00:30:34,312
I'll try contacting them.

527
00:30:34,464 --> 00:30:36,867
[Seo Design]

528
00:30:36,867 --> 00:30:39,167
- They said okay to the redraw.
- I see.

529
00:30:39,167 --> 00:30:42,220
But the client likes
the current Kuranosuke idea,

530
00:30:42,220 --> 00:30:45,224
so we need to propose something
that's even better than that.

531
00:30:49,952 --> 00:30:53,096
Let's see, Nerima...

532
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:55,800
Nerima...

533
00:30:57,568 --> 00:31:00,392
Nerima...

534
00:31:01,900 --> 00:31:05,768
[Revised Character Design]
We need a little more impact.

535
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:08,367
Something like a sense of incongruity.

536
00:31:08,367 --> 00:31:10,240
Incongruity.

537
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:13,400
Understood. I'll revise it immediately.

538
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:15,432
I'm looking forward to it.

539
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:20,467
And regarding the character
for the Nerima shopping mall,

540
00:31:20,467 --> 00:31:23,433
it seems Mr. Seo has been chosen to draw it.

541
00:31:23,433 --> 00:31:25,500
Oh?

542
00:31:25,500 --> 00:31:27,624
Mr. Seo?

543
00:31:31,808 --> 00:31:34,533
[Specialties, Edamame, Nature, Green,
Nerima, Daikon Radish, Komatsuna, Blueberry]

544
00:31:34,533 --> 00:31:37,667
I'm back.

545
00:31:42,567 --> 00:31:44,100
Hello? Yes, this is Kusakabe.

546
00:31:44,100 --> 00:31:48,968
I'm terribly sorry. Really, I'm truly sorry.

547
00:31:52,233 --> 00:31:54,833
Cancelled?

548
00:31:55,400 --> 00:31:57,664
So I'm not allowed to redraw it?

549
00:31:57,664 --> 00:31:59,700
No.

550
00:31:59,700 --> 00:32:02,590
It seems that the plan
to have you draw the Nerima character

551
00:32:02,590 --> 00:32:04,808
has been scrapped entirely.

552
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:07,680
- Why?
- They just said that

553
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:11,240
it was a decision from above.

554
00:32:27,533 --> 00:32:32,072
Hello, Fuchinobe?
There's something I want to ask you.

555
00:32:44,736 --> 00:32:48,328
[Hirose]

556
00:32:52,544 --> 00:32:53,600
What?

557
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:56,500
<i>Oh, Mr. Seo? I'm glad you answered!</i>

558
00:32:56,500 --> 00:32:59,016
<i>Actually, right now...</i>

559
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:35,167
It's been a while, Mr. Omishima.

560
00:33:35,167 --> 00:33:39,667
Yes, it has been a while.
Please, right this way.

561
00:33:50,333 --> 00:33:53,080
Are you Horibe? The one working
the gap part-time job?

562
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:54,080
Well, wait...

563
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:57,120
You, of all days, late today?

564
00:33:57,120 --> 00:33:59,233
- No, I'm not Horibe...
- Anyway, hurry up.

565
00:33:59,233 --> 00:34:01,467
President Omishima is already here.

566
00:34:01,467 --> 00:34:03,000
- What?
- Come on! Hurry!

567
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:04,000
- What?
- Come on!

568
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,000
[Limited-Time Cynical Molco Course]

569
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:09,536
This is amazing.
Collaborating with a restaurant like this.

570
00:34:09,536 --> 00:34:14,567
Officially, it starts tomorrow,
but today is a special occasion.

571
00:34:16,128 --> 00:34:18,440
Excuse me.

572
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:28,200
This is Cynical Molco.
We will be serving your meal shortly.

573
00:34:31,320 --> 00:34:34,733
I think you need a bit more training.

574
00:34:34,733 --> 00:34:36,872
Excuse me.

575
00:34:38,208 --> 00:34:39,733
Are you okay?

576
00:34:39,733 --> 00:34:41,233
Yes, I'm fine.

577
00:34:41,233 --> 00:34:43,600
So hard. So hard. So hard.

578
00:34:43,600 --> 00:34:45,696
Dressing up in mascot costumes is so hard.

579
00:34:45,696 --> 00:34:49,500
It's okay. It's okay. It's hard.

580
00:34:51,733 --> 00:34:54,867
Being here reminds me of eight years ago.

581
00:34:54,867 --> 00:34:57,733
I was launching an electronics company,
and you were my consultant.

582
00:34:57,733 --> 00:34:59,904
Of course, business was booming.

583
00:34:59,904 --> 00:35:02,833
We made a good team, didn't we?

584
00:35:02,833 --> 00:35:07,167
Never imagined I'd run into
my old partner as a rival

585
00:35:07,167 --> 00:35:09,067
in the character creation business.

586
00:35:09,067 --> 00:35:10,933
Rival?

587
00:35:10,933 --> 00:35:13,080
But we're just a team of two people.

588
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:17,640
I'm not so foolish as
to let my guard down around you.

589
00:35:18,120 --> 00:35:23,867
In that case, the rumor
might not be false, then.

590
00:35:23,867 --> 00:35:25,367
Rumor?

591
00:35:25,367 --> 00:35:30,144
Well, the character creation for the Nerima
shopping mall that we were in charge of

592
00:35:30,144 --> 00:35:32,680
was suddenly canceled.

593
00:35:34,100 --> 00:35:35,840
I've heard about that.

594
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:37,533
Of course you have.

595
00:35:37,533 --> 00:35:40,200
Because Merry is the replacement.

596
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:44,352
It pains me to say this,
but it was a request from the client.

597
00:35:44,352 --> 00:35:47,688
There's also one more groundless rumor.

598
00:35:47,833 --> 00:35:51,067
About the character for the Itabashi
shopping mall that your company is handling,

599
00:35:51,067 --> 00:35:53,184
I heard that was also
initially a competition.

600
00:35:53,184 --> 00:35:56,433
But just before the second round of judging,

601
00:35:56,433 --> 00:35:58,467
the competition was abruptly canceled,

602
00:35:58,467 --> 00:36:02,376
- and the replacement was...
- Us, right.

603
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:06,767
Well, both were requests from the clients.

604
00:36:06,767 --> 00:36:09,000
Well, it is just a rumor.

605
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:12,860
But even if it were true,

606
00:36:12,860 --> 00:36:15,080
is there a problem?

607
00:36:15,936 --> 00:36:18,056
No.

608
00:36:18,300 --> 00:36:21,704
It's not against the law.

609
00:36:25,184 --> 00:36:27,496
Excuse me.

610
00:36:28,933 --> 00:36:35,600
However, as a rival in the same industry,

611
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:37,760
I do have one piece of advice.

612
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:42,233
Oh? Please, by all means.

613
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:47,208
Mr. Omishima, your way of doing things...

614
00:36:56,333 --> 00:36:59,240
is killing these little children.

615
00:37:00,767 --> 00:37:03,296
And in the Itabashi competition,

616
00:37:03,296 --> 00:37:07,688
didn't you also kill the children
created by all those designers?

617
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:14,152
I'm sorry, my apologies.

618
00:37:14,267 --> 00:37:17,867
I never imagined that
you would be influenced by Mr. Seo.

619
00:37:17,867 --> 00:37:24,233
That someone like you would call
a mere product a child.

620
00:37:25,067 --> 00:37:29,367
I know, right? I share the same opinion.

621
00:37:34,567 --> 00:37:37,033
But

622
00:37:37,033 --> 00:37:43,667
our way of thinking
isn't always the right answer.

623
00:37:43,667 --> 00:37:46,333
Mr. Seo makes me realize it.

624
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:49,200
Yes?

625
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:54,760
When he's in front of something he loves,
he stops hearing other people's voices,

626
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:59,528
forgets to eat,
and loses track of day and night.

627
00:37:59,968 --> 00:38:04,433
With just that, he attains a happiness
that could reach the heavens,

628
00:38:04,433 --> 00:38:06,888
and if it's taken away,

629
00:38:07,033 --> 00:38:10,696
he'll stake his entire life to get it back.

630
00:38:12,867 --> 00:38:18,267
If a man like Mr. Seo
says that this is his child,

631
00:38:18,267 --> 00:38:21,960
then maybe that's just the truth.

632
00:38:23,267 --> 00:38:25,960
At least, I want to

633
00:38:26,067 --> 00:38:29,576
believe in what Mr. Seo is saying.

634
00:38:31,833 --> 00:38:36,267
- Is that your advice?
- No.

635
00:38:36,267 --> 00:38:43,528
My advice is that I don't want you
to be overconfident, like I once was.

636
00:38:46,100 --> 00:38:49,384
All right, thank you for the meal.
Goodbye, then.

637
00:38:51,633 --> 00:38:55,367
Ms. Kusakabe, you seem to be half asleep.

638
00:38:55,367 --> 00:38:57,576
So...

639
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:09,600
How about this?

640
00:39:09,600 --> 00:39:12,667
Did that wake you up a little?

641
00:39:12,667 --> 00:39:14,167
How far will you go?

642
00:39:14,167 --> 00:39:16,633
Oh, you still seem to be dreaming.

643
00:39:16,633 --> 00:39:20,133
So shall we have a contest? Let's see...

644
00:39:20,133 --> 00:39:22,967
Seo Design, with you as the consultant,
and us, Merry,

645
00:39:22,967 --> 00:39:27,000
competing to see who can create
a new star character first.

646
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:29,933
Let's gather the media
and make it a flashy event.

647
00:39:29,933 --> 00:39:35,533
Of course, the loser will have to
withdraw from this industry.

648
00:39:35,533 --> 00:39:37,700
What do you say?

649
00:39:37,700 --> 00:39:41,800
We'll do it. We'll absolutely do it!

650
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:44,600
If it's come to this, then it's vengeance!
We're going full Kuranosuke on you!

651
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:47,833
Just Mr. Seo and me,
not 47 warriors, just two guys.

652
00:39:47,833 --> 00:39:51,867
We're coming for your head, no, Merry's head!

653
00:39:51,867 --> 00:39:53,633
Interesting.

654
00:39:53,633 --> 00:39:57,667
So, in six months,
let's see whose head will...

655
00:39:57,833 --> 00:40:02,000
Oh, a head! Hey!

656
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:06,632
That saved us an explanation, didn't it?

657
00:40:10,304 --> 00:40:13,467
Mr. Seo, let's do this.

658
00:40:13,467 --> 00:40:15,267
With the blade of our new character,

659
00:40:15,267 --> 00:40:19,267
- we'll take this giant salamander's head!
- I am absolutely not doing it!

660
00:40:19,267 --> 00:40:21,200
Not doing it?

661
00:40:21,200 --> 00:40:24,456
How much more will you insult Molco?

662
00:40:26,467 --> 00:40:28,300
I won't forgive you.

663
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:30,667
No matter what, I will never
forgive you, of all people!

664
00:40:30,667 --> 00:40:33,500
That's right. Let's do it!

665
00:40:33,500 --> 00:40:35,712
- Let's take his head!
- I am absolutely not taking his head!

666
00:40:35,712 --> 00:40:36,733
We won't take it!

667
00:40:36,733 --> 00:40:39,600
What? But what about vengeance?

668
00:40:39,600 --> 00:40:44,072
I won't take vengeance for Molco!

669
00:40:46,592 --> 00:40:48,840
Wait for me, Molco.

670
00:40:49,067 --> 00:40:52,488
I won't let anyone put a stain on you.

671
00:40:55,424 --> 00:40:59,624
If you run away now, won't it be
the same as when you left Merry?

672
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:13,128
Let's compete, Mr. Seo.

673
00:41:14,633 --> 00:41:17,416
You don't understand anything.

674
00:41:18,067 --> 00:41:20,904
It's already settled.

675
00:41:22,900 --> 00:41:29,992
This match is my win by default!

676
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:40,008
Remember that.

677
00:41:52,100 --> 00:41:57,736
Mr. Seo, why? Why not get vengeance?

678
00:42:01,600 --> 00:42:06,833
I mentioned this before.
When I was a kid, I got teased a lot.

679
00:42:06,833 --> 00:42:09,216
They told me it was weird
for a boy to like cute things.

680
00:42:09,216 --> 00:42:14,208
What? That's not weird at all.
What era are you from, the Showa?

681
00:42:14,208 --> 00:42:15,767
Well, but actually,

682
00:42:15,767 --> 00:42:19,620
for a boy to be crazy about
cute things is pretty rare.

683
00:42:19,620 --> 00:42:22,408
Kids can be cruel.

684
00:42:23,033 --> 00:42:25,033
That's true.

685
00:42:25,033 --> 00:42:29,576
And I used to get pretty down about it.

686
00:42:31,567 --> 00:42:34,440
But Berry was always there for me.

687
00:42:36,233 --> 00:42:40,704
Berry never says anything
that gives me a solid push on the back,

688
00:42:40,704 --> 00:42:43,400
like encouragement or anything.

689
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:46,920
Of course, unlike Cynical Molco,

690
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:50,380
she also didn't say things
to brush people off.

691
00:42:50,380 --> 00:42:55,016
She just said "Berry Good".

692
00:42:59,567 --> 00:43:03,944
<i>But with those words...</i>

693
00:43:10,467 --> 00:43:16,680
I know it's kind of late,
but I feel like I've finally figured it out.

694
00:43:16,900 --> 00:43:21,448
What I like,
what I want to create. That's it.

695
00:43:22,020 --> 00:43:25,416
And that's the "cute" I believe in.

696
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:31,100
Thinking about it,
maybe I should be the furthest away from

697
00:43:31,100 --> 00:43:35,600
all that win-or-lose stuff from earlier.

698
00:43:35,733 --> 00:43:37,768
So...

699
00:43:40,067 --> 00:43:42,920
I won't let cuteness be a competition.

700
00:43:48,067 --> 00:43:51,267
I will hate that giant salamander
for all eternity.

701
00:43:51,267 --> 00:43:53,992
- But...
- Cuteness

702
00:43:54,333 --> 00:43:56,840
won't be a competition.

703
00:43:58,800 --> 00:44:00,700
Yeah.

704
00:44:00,700 --> 00:44:04,400
And, at that restaurant,

705
00:44:04,400 --> 00:44:09,067
you went "Bam!" to that
giant salamander for me.

706
00:44:09,067 --> 00:44:12,500
How should I put it...

707
00:44:12,500 --> 00:44:17,216
I'm... just... t-t-thank...

708
00:44:17,216 --> 00:44:20,667
Thank... Thank... Thank...

709
00:44:25,067 --> 00:44:27,767
- Thank...
- How about we go with that?

710
00:44:27,767 --> 00:44:30,100
The thing about our goal.

711
00:44:30,100 --> 00:44:33,920
Free from winning or losing,
with no heavy message or weird twists.

712
00:44:33,920 --> 00:44:37,233
And yet, it supports someone.
It just supports them.

713
00:44:37,233 --> 00:44:40,767
Let's create a character
with that kind of concept.

714
00:44:40,767 --> 00:44:43,240
Just supporting.

715
00:44:44,600 --> 00:44:50,133
Let's just make what you've always loved!

716
00:44:56,733 --> 00:44:59,367
As expected of me.

717
00:44:59,367 --> 00:45:01,533
- What?
- It's obvious, isn't it?

718
00:45:01,533 --> 00:45:03,456
You've got that
"I thought of it myself" face,

719
00:45:03,456 --> 00:45:05,120
but that was pretty much all me.

720
00:45:05,120 --> 00:45:07,808
- Well, you're not wrong, but...
- Brazenly taking credit.

721
00:45:07,808 --> 00:45:10,579
You are really the successor of hyena-ism.

722
00:45:10,579 --> 00:45:14,433
And you committed
another violation, didn't you?

723
00:45:14,433 --> 00:45:17,056
[Touch the cute here, and you're fired]
Bringing out Molco without permission, huh?

724
00:45:17,056 --> 00:45:22,312
Well, this time it's a special exception.

725
00:45:23,776 --> 00:45:27,200
I'll forgive you if you go buy this.

726
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:29,567
[Very Popular Daitaidou Nikanaru]
It's a detergent called Daitaidou Nikanaru.

727
00:45:29,567 --> 00:45:32,064
It's supposed to be good for
stains on stuffed animals too.

728
00:45:32,064 --> 00:45:34,567
Well, maybe next time.

729
00:45:34,567 --> 00:45:36,500
No, now, okay?

730
00:45:36,500 --> 00:45:38,900
I have to get the stain out.

731
00:45:38,900 --> 00:45:40,800
Now? Now?

732
00:45:40,800 --> 00:45:41,888
But it's already nighttime.

733
00:45:41,888 --> 00:45:43,300
And besides, I don't even know
where they sell it.

734
00:45:43,300 --> 00:45:46,667
You know what?
If you're sorry, just go look for it.

735
00:45:46,667 --> 00:45:49,333
And if you're not, you won't.
Now which is it?

736
00:45:49,333 --> 00:45:53,960
You'll go! You're sorry! Go! Run, run!

737
00:45:57,139 --> 00:46:01,472
I think I can somehow manage!

738
00:46:01,472 --> 00:46:04,392
Just supporting.

739
00:46:12,416 --> 00:46:15,296
Make it happen!

740
00:46:15,296 --> 00:46:17,768
I'm fed up!
